@meta
id: 17-13
title: Drill — mark, leave, return
chapter: 17
type: drill
skills: marks-set, marks-jump, mark-backtick
par: 38
minutes: 5
reps: 8
vscode: Ctrl+K Ctrl+K to bookmark, if the extension is installed
open: release-notes.md

@brief
Eight times: the `Unreleased` heading becomes `2.4.0`, and the stray
`<!-- draft -->` line at the very bottom goes.

Find `Unreleased`, mark it, go to the bottom, delete the line, come
back to the mark and change the word. The mark has to be on the word,
not the line, or you will be changing `##`.

@keys
| `ma` | mark here |
| `` `a `` | back to the marked character |
| `G` `dd` | last line, delete it |
| `ciw` | change the word |

@hints
The search leaves you on the `U`. Mark before you move.
--
`` `a `` with the backtick puts you back on the `U`, so `ciw` changes
the right word. `'a` would put you on the first `#`.

@solution
    /Unreleased<Enter> ma G dd `a ciw2.4.0<Esc> :wq<Enter>

Set, leave, return. Once this is a reflex you will find yourself
dropping `ma` before any excursion, the way you would put a finger in
a book before flipping to the index. It costs two keystrokes and it
never fails, whereas `Ctrl-O` occasionally surprises you when you have
jumped more times than you thought.

Lowercase marks belong to the file. Every buffer has its own `a`, so
setting `a` in the release notes does not disturb an `a` you set in a
provider earlier. The next lessons use that, and then break it on
purpose with the uppercase ones.

@start release-notes.md
# Release notes

## Unreleased

- Refund window enforced at 30 days
- Duplicate refund guard in PaymentService
- Order confirmation email moved to a template

## 2.3.0

- Partial refunds
- Customer lookup by email
- Fix double email on order creation

## 2.2.1

- Fix cancelled orders showing as shipped in the export
- Pin tsyringe to 4.8
<!-- draft -->

